  "notes": "Campaign B1 unit (gendn-xpz) for a legacy-unassessed page: the page carried zero id attributes, so no selector could resolve to it. Six existing headings gained ids — four <h2> (at-a-glance, why-it-exists, relation-to-existing-gamepad-api, browser-support) and two <h3> (gamepad-event on 'rawgamepadinputchange event', example on 'Event-driven input loop (replaces polling)'). The <h3> ids are necessary because fragmentAfterId() slices to the next <h1-3>: the 'shape of the API' and 'example' <h2>s each have an <h3> immediately inside, so an id on those <h2>s would resolve to an empty fragment. The page already contained a <pre><code> example block, so none was added, and no prose was reworded or added. SOURCES RE-FETCHED, NOT ASSUMED (2026-10-06). CARRIED DISAGREEMENTS — BOTH SIDES STATED, NEITHER ADJUDICATED: (1) The page's 'shape of the API' citation and #at-a-glance cite the 'W3C Gamepad spec (working draft)' as the source of the rawgamepadinputchange event and its shape, but fetched 2026-10-06 the spec at w3c.github.io/gamepad contains zero occurrences of 'rawgamepadinputchange'; its defined events are gamepadconnected/gamepaddisconnected, and its 'Other events' note lists future 'gamepadchanged'/'gamepadaxischanged' as 'more discussion needed'. The event name appears in the ChromeStatus record 5989275208253440 summary (and in the Microsoft Edge explainer, which this page does not link). (2) The page's #at-a-glance says to enable chrome://flags/#enable-experimental-web-platform-features, but fetched 2026-10-06 the ChromeStatus record's flag_name is '#gamepad-raw-input-change-event' with flag:false. (3) The page labels the feature 'In developer trial (behind a flag)', while fetched 2026-10-06 the ChromeStatus record reads browser status 'In development' (val 3), intent_stage 'Start incubating', flag:false, origintrial:false. The page's Firefox/Safari 'No signal' and Firefox experimental-implementation note match the record's ff/safari views (fetched 2026-10-06). No divergence is pinned here: the implementer owns divergence disclosure and pinning in scripts/source-disagreement.test.mjs. IN-UNIT PROSE REPAIR (coord 22:30Z): the divergences above are now disclosed ON THE PAGE, both sides with their values and the fetch date inside the sentence, and pinned in the curated table in scripts/source-disagreement.test.mjs. VERIFIED BY THE IMPLEMENTER before the page carried any of it: fetching https://w3c.github.io/gamepad/ returns 200 and contains ZERO occurrences of rawgamepadinputchange (it carries gamepadconnected, gamepaddisconnected, and future-tense gamepadchanged/gamepadaxischanged), so the page's attribution of that name to the spec is unsupported; ChromeStatus 5989275208253440 reads name \"Gamepad Event-Driven Input API\", status \"In development\", intent_stage \"Start incubating\", flag_name \"#gamepad-raw-input-change-event\", and NO desktop milestone - so the page's \"In developer trial\" in Chrome 147 is not what the record says. | 2026-11-08 factual fix + MDN-shape upgrade: the documented event name rawgamepadinputchange (from the ChromeStatus summary) is wrong — Chromium registers and dispatches gamepadrawinputchanged (event_type_names.json5, navigator_gamepad.cc) and the explainer and ChromeStatus sample demo agree. The page now documents the real surface from Chromium IDL: GamepadRawInputChangeEvent (+constructor), five FrozenArray<long> index attributes, GamepadRawInputChangeEventInit, ongamepadrawinputchanged. Constructor behaviour browser-verified in Chrome 153 with --enable-blink-features=GamepadRawInputChangeEvent. Inventory ids rawgamepadinputchange-event/gamepad-snapshot kept for continuity. The CPS showcase demo is not embedded because it listens for the stale name."
